{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":31,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmo_baryon_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmo_baryon_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L397-L402","doc":"**So the baryon GMO combination also takes every value.** Immediate from\nsurjectivity; stated because it is the claim the retraction is about. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.baryon_octet_second_order_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.baryon_octet_second_order_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":378,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L378-L395","doc":"**Any four baryon-octet masses are attainable at second order.** This is the\nretraction made precise: the baryon octet is surjective just as the meson octet\nis, so baryon GMO is *also* vacuous at second order.\n\nNote the witness needs `b ≠ 0` where the meson one did not — the baryon octet\nhas four independent masses rather than three, because `N` and `Ξ` are not\ncharge-conjugate partners. That extra mass is exactly matched by the extra\nstructure, which is why the rank still saturates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.baryon_octet_g_absorbed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.baryon_octet_g_absorbed","kind":"theorem","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L368-L376","doc":"**On the baryon octet too, `g` is a disguised `b`** — the same `Y·fourD = 2Y`\ncollapse, since hypercharge `±1` forces `I = 1/2` in either octet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmo_baryon_second_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmo_baryon_second_order","kind":"theorem","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L362-L366","doc":"**The baryon combination has the same second-order value as the meson one**,\n`16(4e − 3f)` — `g` cancels here too. The two octets carry the same `(I, Y)`\npattern (`π ↔ Σ`, `η ↔ Λ`, `K⁺ ↔ N`, `K⁻ ↔ Ξ`), so this is not a coincidence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmoBaryon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmoBaryon","kind":"def","line":357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L357-L360","doc":"The baryon GMO combination `2(m_N + m_Ξ) − 3m_Λ − m_Σ`, i.e. the doubled form\nof `(m_N + m_Ξ)/2 = (3m_Λ + m_Σ)/4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.xiB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.xiB","kind":"def","line":354,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L354-L355","doc":"`Ξ`: `I = 1/2, Y = −1` ⇒ `fourD = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.sigmaB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.sigmaB","kind":"def","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L352-L353","doc":"`Σ`: `I = 1, Y = 0` ⇒ `fourD = 8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lambdaB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lambdaB","kind":"def","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L350-L351","doc":"`Λ`: `I = 0, Y = 0` ⇒ `fourD = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.nucleon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.nucleon","kind":"def","line":348,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L348-L349","doc":"Nucleon: `I = 1/2, Y = 1` ⇒ `fourD = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmo_combination_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmo_combination_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L276-L282","doc":"**The GMO combination takes every value.** Immediate from surjectivity, and\nworth stating on its own: there is no value of the deviation that would count as\nevidence for or against a second-order term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.meson_octet_second_order_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.meson_octet_second_order_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L259-L274","doc":"**Any three meson-octet masses are attainable at second order.** Given\ntargets `p, h, k` for pion, eta and kaon, explicit coefficients reproduce all\nthree — and the kaon doublet stays degenerate, since the witness has `b = g = 0`.\n\nHence the Gell-Mann–Okubo relation, which is an identity at first order\n(`GellMannOkuboIdentity`), is **vacuous** at second order: its combination can\ntake any value at all, so matching the observed ≈ 6 % deviation constrains\nnothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.decuplet_g_absorbed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.decuplet_g_absorbed","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L224-L233","doc":"**On the decuplet, `g` is a disguised `b` and `e`.** Shifting\n`b ↦ b + 2g` and `e ↦ e + 3g/2` reproduces every decuplet mass with `g = 0`.\nThe shift in `e` is exactly the `6g` visible in `decuplet_second_order`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.meson_octet_g_absorbed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.meson_octet_g_absorbed","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L214-L222","doc":"**On the octet, `g` is a disguised `b`.** Shifting `b ↦ b + g/2` reproduces\nevery meson-octet mass with `g = 0`. Exact, all four states. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.decuplet_zero_gmo_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.decuplet_zero_gmo_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L176-L186","doc":"And one with a **nonzero** GMO deviation and **zero** decuplet one. So the\ntwo relations constrain genuinely different combinations.\n\nThe leftover freedom is **not** a missing physical constraint — see\n`meson_octet_g_absorbed` and `decuplet_g_absorbed` below, which show `g` is\nabsorbed exactly by the lower-order coefficients on both multiplets. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmo_zero_decuplet_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmo_zero_decuplet_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L168-L174","doc":"A second-order term with **zero** GMO deviation and a **nonzero** decuplet\none. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.decuplet_second_differences_equal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.decuplet_second_differences_equal","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L156-L162","doc":"**But the failure is uniform.** The two second differences remain *exactly*\nequal, so the decuplet goes from linear to exactly quadratic in the ladder\nposition with no cubic residue — a constraint testable independently of the\ncommon size of the deviation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.decuplet_second_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.decuplet_second_order","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L150-L154","doc":"**The equal-spacing rule fails at second order** — each second difference is\n`8·(4e + 9f + 6g)`, nonzero in general. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.spacingLower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.spacingLower","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L147-L148","doc":"Lower second difference `Ξ* − 2Σ* + Δ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.spacingUpper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.spacingUpper","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L144-L146","doc":"Upper second difference `Ω − 2Ξ* + Σ*`; zero iff the top three are equally\nspaced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.omega","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.omega","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L141-L142","doc":"Ω: `I = 0, Y = −2` ⇒ `fourD = −4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.xiStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.xiStar","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L139-L140","doc":"Ξ*: `I = 1/2, Y = −1` ⇒ `fourD = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.sigmaStar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.sigmaStar","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L137-L138","doc":"Σ*: `I = 1, Y = 0` ⇒ `fourD = 8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.delta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.delta","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L135-L136","doc":"Δ: `I = 3/2, Y = 1` ⇒ `fourD = 14`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmo_blind_to_Yd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmo_blind_to_Yd","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L123-L128","doc":"**GMO is blind to the `Y·d` structure.** Changing `g` freely leaves the\ncombination unchanged — it is odd in `Y` and cancels in the kaon average. So a\nfit to the GMO deviation cannot constrain `g`, even in principle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmo_second_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmo_second_order","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L117-L121","doc":"**GMO at second order is `16·(4e − 3f)`.** It vanishes identically in the\nfirst-order parameters `a, b, c` — recovering `GellMannOkuboIdentity` — and\npicks up exactly one combination of the second-order ones. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmoCombination","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.gmoCombination","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L112-L115","doc":"The GMO combination `4·⟨m²_K⟩ − 3·m²_η − m²_π`, doubled so the hypercharge\naverage over the kaon doublet needs no division. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.kaonMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.kaonMinus","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L109-L110","doc":"Kaon at `Y = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.kaonPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.kaonPlus","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L107-L108","doc":"Kaon at `Y = +1`: `I = 1/2` ⇒ `fourD = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.eta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.eta","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L105-L106","doc":"Eta: `I = 0, Y = 0` ⇒ `fourD = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.pion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.pion","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L103-L104","doc":"Pion: `I = 1, Y = 0` ⇒ `fourD = 8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.m16","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.m16","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GellMannOkuboSecondOrder.lean#L91-L98","doc":"`16 ×` the mass of a state, with first-order coefficients `a, b, c` and\nsecond-order `e` (`Y²`), `f` (`d²`), `g` (`Y·d`).\n\n`fourD = 4·I(I+1) − Y²`, i.e. `4d`. The `16 ×` and the `fourD` parametrisation\nbetween them clear every denominator; both scalings are uniform across states\nand cancel from every combination below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}